    "created_at": "2026-03-09T14:42:59Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-03-09T14:42:59Z",
    "body": "I'm a little confused because my initial interpretation would be that fragment parsing should not have a custom element registry to keep elements from being upgraded during fragment parsing. \n\nBut then @AtkinsSJ expects differently:\n\n> By default its custom element registry is null. I believe it should be set here to the context element's document's custom element registry.\n\n[Fragment parsing step 7.](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/parsing.html#parsing-html-fragments) already says \"and context's [custom element registry](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#element-custom-element-registry).\", so it seems this is per your expectations?\n\nDid this change between you filing this issue and today? Perhaps @annevk has some context here.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
